 "connect": {
  "_about": "Melomania Connect 2.6.0 (A100, A100 SE, M100, P100, P100 SE, X100; docs/cambridge/PROTOCOL.md section 9): Qualcomm GAIA v3 with Cambridge's custom API. A frame is FF, version 3, flags (1 checksum, 2 length extension), the payload length, the vendor, the command word and the payload, with an XOR byte when the checksum flag is set. The command word is feature << 9 | type << 7 | command (type: 0 command, 1 notification, 2 response, 3 error). Read from devices/gaia3/customapi in the app; ids are the app's enums. The EQ is Qualcomm's music processing feature (vendor 001D, feature 5; QTIL v3), which the app drives through its bundled gaiaclient library: the earbuds hold one user set of bands (frequency, Q, filter, gain in 1/60 dB); the app's presets are lists of band gains (RemoteConfigDefault.json in the APK) that it writes to that user set. Each model's `config` is the app's LocalConfig/DeviceConfig (which controls it shows) and `eq_presets` its bundled RemoteConfigDefault.json. Touch actions are Qualcomm's gesture configuration feature (vendor 001D, feature 11; V3GestureConfigurationPlugin): a configuration is 16 bits, touchpad << 14 | context << 7 | action, listed per gesture; the app's assign screen offers tap, double tap, triple tap (swipe up) and long press per earbud with play/pause, next, previous, volume up and down, next noise mode, voice assistant (push to talk) or nothing. GET_DEVICES (22) is answered with one frame per paired device: id, name (20 bytes, NUL padded), four address bytes, connection status (peer); the app collects the frames for two seconds, and CONNECT_DEVICE/DISCONNECT_DEVICE (23, 24) take the id.",
